  "question": {
    "text": "A triangle has two of its vertices at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in the Cartesian plane. Its third vertex lies on the <math><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. If the area of the triangle is <math><mn>2</mn></math> square units, then the sum of the square of the possible values of abscissa of the third vertex is",
    "image": null
